{"type":"message","id":"f9cff623","parentId":"98a67719","timestamp":"2026-05-17T12:47:35.749Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Cloudflare error 1101 is \"Worker rejected request\" - this typically means there's a runtime error in the Cloudflare Worker. This is an application-level error, not an auth error. Since GET works fine but POST fails with 1101, it seems the POST endpoint has a bug in the Worker.\n\nThe Worker is rejecting POST requests at the runtime level. There's likely a bug in the `/send` endpoint of the Worker code.\n\nLet me check what the API supports more carefully. The 1101 is a Workers-specific error. Maybe I need to include additional required fields, or the endpoint expects a different payload format.\n\nLet me try with the message as the top-level field instead of inside content:\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-3c5ed4cc-c17f-4c31-98d9-8a12588621c8","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try different payload formats\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"message\":\"**[Heartbeat 12:45 UTC]\"}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":2710,"output":248,"cacheRead":17744,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20702,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779022044889,"responseId":"chatcmpl-53dca60d-540d-4ae5-9b6f-00181d4a0b70"}}
